WEBVTT

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.620
This tale is set at the end
of the second century.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.410
The warrior Kan'u, with her beautiful,
flowing long black hair

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.910
and her deadly blade Seiryuu Engetsutou, sets out
to defeat the evil plaguing the war-ravaged lands.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.360
Tied to her, by sisterhood's
tight bonds, is Chouhi.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.750
And a strange destiny delivers to them

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:29.250
Chou'un, Bachou, Kouchuu,
and Shokatsu Koumei.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.200
The tale woven by these unparalleled
warrior princesses begins again now!

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.480
You bandits who attack defenseless villages,
I, Kin Bachou, shall be your opponent!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.750
Rin Rin-sama coming through!

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.880
Out of the way!

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.680
Come on out, General!

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.330
Fight with Rin Rin!

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.790
Damn! We can't even move.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.970
If we don't do something, the
vanguard's gonna collapse.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.560
They lured us into this small
valley to trap us!

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.000
Temporary retreat!

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.010
Get to a larger, open space
and counterattack!

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.350
Hey, don't run away!

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.440
Everybody, follow them!

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.560
Chouhi, wait.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.970
Why stop me?

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.360
Now's our chance!

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.990
Did you forget Koumei's plan?

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.840
Oh, right...

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.570
Let's leave the rest to everyone else.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.690
Yeah.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.570
Koumei-chan was right.
They're running straight past us.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.090
Bandits!

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.100
Throw down your weapons and surrender.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.000
If you don't, you will fall prey to my bow!

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.980
Boss, an ambush!

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.830
Damn, they tricked us.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.530
Now!

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.600
<i>Run!</i>

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.940
I, Chou Shiryuu, shall lead you to hell!

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.380
We're the only ones left...

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.780
Shut up!

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.860
Boss. Look up ahead.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.200
Ka... That's a Kan flag, right?

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.070
Which means...

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.290
<i>Ah! Kan'u!</i>

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.250
You bandits who use the wars to
further oppress the people...

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.470
Your blood will stain my
Seiryuu Engetsutou!

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:15.460
Nearly all the bandits infesting this area
have been defeated. Wonderful!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.480
It's all thanks to you, and
we're ever so grateful!

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.760
I, the village head, was especially impressed
by the many stratagems

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.820
of Koumei - a true equal to the legendary
Chinpei, who saved Emperor Ryuuhou,

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.730
becoming a cornerstone
of the Han Dynasty!

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.960
Oh, not at all...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.420
Don't be so humble.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:40.670
He's right. Our army does indeed owe
much of its victory to your tactics.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:47.130
I am a bit unhappy that Aisha took
so many of the good parts.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:52.570
With Kan'u-dono, Chou'un-dono, Bachou-dono,
and Kouchuu-dono,

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:55.930
great warriors truly fill the
Touka Village army!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.270
You didn't include Rin Rin!

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.770
Even among those,

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.140
the sight of Chouhi-dono racing her pig about
the battlefield was awe-inspiring,

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:07.810
and I'm told the men have dubbed
you "The Mighty Pig General."

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.930
Don't praise me so much! I'm blushing...

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.250
It's wide-open!

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.240
Bachou, give back my dumpling!

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.170
I already ate it.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.520
Both of you, that's bad manners!

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.550
But Shuri-

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.460
Riri-chan's watching!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.550
S-Sorry. Jeez...

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:31.930
Fine.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.130
Rin Rin-chan, there's something
on your cheek.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.360
Stop it, Shuri.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.060
I can do it myself!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.950
Rin Rin-oneechan's like a little kid!

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.730
Hey, Riri!

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:49.070
You shouldn't use somebody's given name without
permission, no matter how close you are.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.240
Call her "Chouhi-oneechan."

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.710
But Rin Rin-oneechan always
calls herself "Rin Rin"!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.330
That's irrelevant.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.440
If you use it without asking,
you deserve whatever she says to you.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.170
I really don't mind!

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:09.580
You're like family to me now, so you
can use my given name, Rin Rin!

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.650
Isn't that nice, Riri?

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:12.330
Yeah!

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.270
Rin Rin-oneechan, I love you!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.180
<b>Chapter 1
Bachou's Anguish</b>

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:26.120
After wiping out bandits, a bath is great!

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.150
The food at the banquet was
perfect, life's wonderful...

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:36.120
It was so funny when Riri said that
Chouhi was like a little girl.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.850
Rin Rin-chan, there's something
on your cheek.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.890
Stop it, Shuri.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:47.370
When did Chouhi start calling Koumei by her given name?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:50.390
She didn't do it when I first got here...

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:54.350
And why won't she do that with me?

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.260
We're companions!

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.160
Friends!

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.800
<i>War buddies!</i>

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.440
No, wait. Calm down.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.880
I don't use her given name, either...

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:10.300
That's right... There just hasn't been
a good time for me to use it yet. 

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:14.330
But it'd be kind of embarrassing
to ask her now.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.230
OK!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.940
When I get out, I'll call her "Rin Rin"!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:29.590
Maybe she'll be like, "Since you're using my given
name, I'll start calling you by yours, Sui!"

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.490
Yeah!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:35.850
Man, I was so focused on thinking, I spent
a little too much time in the hot bath.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.340
Bachou!

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.510
How was your bath?

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.620
I-It was great.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.100
Then I'll take one, too!

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.620
This is the perfect chance!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.080
I'll just nonchalantly say, "Rin Rin."

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.430
Hey, Rin...

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.090
What?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:59.740
Rin... Rin... Rin... Rin...

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.710
Unless you tell me, I won't
know what you want!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.330
It's nothing!

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.020
Really! Nothing!

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:10.740
Silly Bachou.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:17.130
Bath, bath, bath! There's a
bath, so I'm gonna take it!

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:25.060
I think it'd be cuter with thicker eyebrows...
Oh, and I forgot the hair ornament!

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.520
Done!

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.650
That's it!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.580
I think it looks pretty good.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.980
Just like her!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.690
Yeah. You can't just barge into it.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:39.430
First, I've gotta pretend this is her,
and then practice her given name.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.960
Ri... Ri... Ri... Ri!

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.090
This is pretty tough.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.050
Hey, Chouhi!

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:01.500
That's pretty easy to say.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.210
I'll try saying her given name like this.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.230
Yo, Ri... Ri... Ri-

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.720
Rin Rin-oneechan!

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.990
Kan'u-san! Good night!

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.090
Good night!

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.180
Good night!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.680
Let's play Kemari tomorrow!

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:15.520
Yeah!

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.180
Ri... Riri...

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.210
Ri... Ri...

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:31.750
Bachou was acting odd?

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:37.950
Yeah. Last night, when Riri passed by
Bachou-san and Koumei-san's room,

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:43.220
she heard a strange voice coming through the door,
which was open a crack. So she looked to see...

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:48.190
She was using her fingers to
climb the stairs to heaven?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.430
That wouldn't really bother me.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.860
Um, Kouchuu-dono?

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.630
Actually, she had some strange
talisman on her bed,

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.330
and she was kneeling before
it and muttering something.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.120
She ate a decent amount for dinner
before returning to her room,

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.810
but she didn't seem that hungry
today, which is rare for her.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:13.850
She didn't seem to sleep too
well last night, either.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:17.050
And she spent most of today in her room...

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:20.560
Perhaps she has some kind of depression.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.800
What?! She's sick?

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.690
From what I've heard,

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:27.990
the people of Seiryou charge on their
horses across vast, open plains,

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:33.240
and any prey they capture, they eat raw,
starting with the head.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:38.170
Thus, perhaps life here in the
village isn't suited to her.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.540
Hey, hey. Don't blame me if you get letters
of complaint from the Seiryou people.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.860
Chou'un-san's fairytales aside,

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:50.920
it's quite common for a change of environment
to produce a gradual accumulation

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.520
of negative feelings within a person's heart,
which they aren't even aware of.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:59.450
If that's the case, perhaps it would be best if she
returned to her village and rested for a while.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.740
Let's not jump to conclusions. Let's
just see how things go for a bit.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.380
Right.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.360
Yo, Ran Ran...

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.320
Yo, Run Run!

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.770
Yo, Ri... Ri... Ri...

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:20.850
I can say "Ran Ran" and "Run Run."
Why can't I say it?

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:23.320
I'm taking a break!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.710
You're like family to me now, so you
can use my given name, Rin Rin!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:33.290
Then you could use my given name, too.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:39.260
Or maybe she doesn't think
of me that way...

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.160
Bachou.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.460
Wh-What...

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.340
What's up?

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.130
I want to talk for a second.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.880
Ta-Talk about what, Ri... Ri... Ri-

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.630
You should go back to Seiryou!

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:02.150
Everybody's saying it isn't good for
you here, so you should go back.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.400
What do you mean?

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:07.790
You're all better off with me gone?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:12.100
No, I was just thinking it'd be
better for you to go back-

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:13.150
That's the same thing!

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:14.610
No, it isn't!

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.180
Then how is it different?!

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:22.270
Well, um... Going home does
mean you aren't here.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.480
But it's not that it's better
that you're not here-

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:25.380
Get out!

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.430
What do mean, get out?

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.610
I'm worried about you!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.600
Shut up! Shut up Shut up!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.950
I don't want to listen to you!

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.790
Get out! Get out!

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.190
Fine! I'll leave!

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.830
Bachou-san, are you...

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:01.870
More!                             More!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:03.640
Hmph!                            Hmph!

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:11.730
I'm done!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.370
U-Um, did you want any more?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.520
Rin Rin-oneechan?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.890
What?

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:37.230
Did you get into a fight
with Bachou-oneechan?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.040
I-It's got nothing to do with a kid like you!

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.230
I see how it is!

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:48.390
And I was going to tell you how to go back
to being friends with her again, too!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.820
What? How?

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.390
Do you want me to tell you?

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.820
I do, I do.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:55.230
Then, I'll tell you!

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:59.480
First, you kiss her on the cheek, OK?

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.200
And then...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:06.220
When my dad was still alive,
he would fight with my mom.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.690
But when he did that, they
made up right away!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.630
Then, Rin Rin and Bachou can...

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.430
...definitely get back together like that!

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:19.110
So go make up with her,
and play with me some more!

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:20.530
Got it!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:27.450
Maybe I should go back to Seiryou...

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.630
There you are!

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:34.170
Bachou!

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.420
Hey, Bachou!

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:36.970
What?!

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.390
Bachou...

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.010
Wh-What?

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.120
Bachou.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.450
Stupid!

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:55.150
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid! Stupid! <i>Stupid!</i>

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.080
Why?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.680
Why did she suddenly do that?

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:02.880
Why? Why?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:08.770
Damn it! I don't know what's going on anymore,
and my head feels ready to explode! I just...

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.740
Jeez... That didn't work at all.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:18.140
I did what she told me, and
it just made things worse!

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.690
This is why you can't trust what kids say.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.610
Bachou-san is late...

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:31.800
Bachou-san may have been late some other times,
but she's never, ever been late for dinner.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:36.740
Perhaps she collapsed in the mountains and
another three-day flower grew on her.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:40.790
Chou'un-san, don't say
crazy things like that!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:44.300
Well, knowing her, she's probably all right.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:48.700
But she did seem strange this morning...

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:52.380
Still, no matter how much she's
suffering from depression,

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.170
she's not the type to go into the
mountains to hang herself.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.320
The mountains?

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.670
That's true...

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.560
I'm going to go look for her!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.550
Look for her? Where?

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:03.650
H-Hey!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.280
Hey, Bachou!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.390
Where are you?

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:14.410
Say something if you can hear me!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.180
Bachou!

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:17.670
Ouch...

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:19.640
Don't hang yourself!

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.910
...the hell?

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:27.220
Since she ran into the mountains, I thought
I could find her if I looked in the mountains.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.420
But I can't find her!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.510
Man, her search is sloppy, as usual.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.150
That's...

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:38.550
Dang! Since it's Bachou we're talking about,
I should've brought food to lure her out.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.780
Rin Rin, watch out!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.290
Bachou!

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.030
Behind you!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:47.270
Behind you, Rin Rin!

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.210
Behind me?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.530
Kan Kan!

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.570
It's Kan Kan!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.900
Hey, Rin Rin. Who's Kan Kan?

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:04.590
Kan Kan was a boar Rin Rin used to keep!

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.960
He had lived with me ever
since I was really little.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:13.500
But my grandpa said I had to send him back
to the mountains when he grew up.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.270
so I said my teary goodbye to him.

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.750
I never thought I'd see him here.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.130
What a tearful reunion!

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:24.590
That's fine, but are you sure it's
the one you used to have?

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:25.990
Sure, I am.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:30.400
Look. He's got a white patch
right near his front leg...

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:34.790
He doesn't...

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:38.120
Looks like I got the wrong boar...

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.560
<i>Run!</i>

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.980
What kind of "tearful reunion" was that?!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:54.080
Th-That's just the nature of when regrets
well up like that. It can't be helped.

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:56.380
What the heck?

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:00.480
Jeez... This is why Rin Rin...

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:05.220
What? I just started calling Chouhi "Rin Rin"...

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:10.530
H-Hey... I...

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:14.210
I'm calling you by your given
name, Rin Rin. Is that OK?

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.170
If you want to do that, Bachou, that's fine.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.580
Because you're my friend!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:29.190
Yeah, that's right!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.400
We're friends!

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.990
What's so funny?

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:35.850
Why are you laughing?

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.710
Sorry, but...

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.130
What?

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.190
Tell me what you're laughing at!

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.730
Aw, who cares?

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.160
We're friends. Don't worry about it!

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:57.030
Want to go back to everyone, Rin Rin?

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:58.470
Yeah.

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.170
I see. So that's what it was?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:09.630
Jeez. You caused all this trouble over that?

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.830
I don't mind.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.140
It kind of makes you smile.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:18.720
But Rin Rin, why don't you call
Bachou by her given name?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.060
Because Sei said

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:26.500
that if somebody who isn't a relative calls somebody from
Seiryou by their given name, they turn into a horse.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:30.520
I didn't want Bachou to turn into a horse...

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.160
A horse?

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.910
Really?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.940
That's not true, is it, Mom?

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.660
<i>Chou'un!</i>

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.780
Um... sorry. Sorry.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.160
I was just playing around. I didn't
think it would get this big.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.730
Jeez, Chou'un's at fault for lying,

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:51.400
but I can't believe you'd fall for something
that not even Riri-chan believes!

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:57.750
If she had just asked innocently, like she did when
she heard mine, this never would've happened.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:05.260
Also, when I started calling you Sei, she was really
persistent in saying that she wanted to as well.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.770
I wanted to be like Aisha for everything!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:13.240
Hey, how about we all share
our given names again?

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.200
Great!

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.740
Let's do it!

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:17.690
No objections.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.220
That sounds nice.

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.050
Me too! Me too!

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:26.940
But I don't think I really want to call someone that
much older than I am by their given name...

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:29.740
Kan'u-san, what are you getting at here?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.250
N-Never mind! Nothing.

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:35.810
Then I'll start.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.450
My name is Kan'u. My style name is Unchou.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:39.580
My given name is Aisha.

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:41.510
I give my name to all of you!

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.200
Rin Rin is Chouhi!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.590
My style name is Yokutoku.

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:46.640
My given name is Rin Rin, of course!

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.730
I give my name to all of you!

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:50.410
I am Bachou!

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:51.570
My style name is Mouki!

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.610
My given name is Sui!

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.940
I give it to all of you!

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:55.660
My name is Chou'un.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:56.950
My style name is Shiryuu.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.070
My given name is Sei.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.910
I wish to give it to all of you.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:01.640
I'm Shokatsu Ryou.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:02.780
My style name is Koumei.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.970
My given name is Shuri.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:05.980
I give my name to all-

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:08.310
I am Kouchuu.

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.870
My style name is Kanshou.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.970
My given name is Shion.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.260
I give my name to all of you.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.080
I am Riri!

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.660
With these bonds of our
friendship deepened,

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:23.880
let us now fight harder for the
land and all its people!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.060
Yeah!

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:01.060
What's wrong?

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.390
Can't sleep?

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:06.320
No, that's not it.

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:09.720
It's peaceful.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:10.820
Yeah.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:12.310
But...

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:14.540
Is something bothering you?

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:17.920
This area has indeed become peaceful.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:21.530
But, there are still people out there who suffer.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:26.910
When I think of that, I wonder
if it's truly OK to stay here...

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:31.380
Going on another journey?

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:34.850
Yeah, that might be a good idea.

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:39.310
I'm sure you already know, but when
you do go, I'll be with you.

00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:44.060
That's fine, but don't vanish midway again.

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:46.460
Rin Rin's going, too!

00:23:47.510 --> 00:23:53.810
Rin Rin will be with Aisha forever...
Forever... Forever...

00:23:57.650 --> 00:23:59.800
A journey, huh?

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.760
Um, excuse me.

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.080
What is it?

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:08.190
Uh, how do I get to Touka Village?

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:09.750
Touka Village?

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:12.040
Oh, where the peasant army is?

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:13.040
Yes.

00:24:26.590 --> 00:24:30.330
Rin Rin, explain the <i>Romance of the Three Kingdoms.</i>

00:24:30.330 --> 00:24:35.820
In the <i>Romance of the Three Kingdoms</i>, Rin Rin and the
rest go to India, along with a powerful priest, to get a sutra!

00:24:35.820 --> 00:24:40.030
Oh... So, you're the monkey, and I'm the kappa?

00:24:40.030 --> 00:24:40.930
Wait a second.

00:24:40.930 --> 00:24:42.430
Does that make me the pig?

00:24:42.430 --> 00:24:43.640
The sow?

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:46.910
I'm not sure that's what you were
supposed to get upset over...

00:24:46.910 --> 00:24:49.640
Next time on <i>Shin Koihime Musou,</i> Episode 2:

00:24:49.640 --> 00:24:51.880
Ryuubi Visits Touka Village!

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:55.060
<b>Episode 2
Ryuubi Visits
Touka Village</b>

00:24:51.880 --> 00:24:55.040
Hey, who's that just now?

00:24:55.050 --> 00:25:00.020
<b>Watch us again, OK?
And rewatch this episode!</b>
